--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUMMARY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI EnergyProductsPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure @Observable
state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/empty/error/success over an injectable
EnergyProductsDataSource seam (default = a Powerwall+Solar SI sample), plus a lazily-loaded per-site
configuration cache (web useTeslaEnergySiteInfo) with its own loading/success/empty states. Adaptive layout
(macOS/iPad two-column site grid vs iPhone single column) using the P2 tokens + P3 shared components —
TSGlassPanel/TSCard/TSStatCard/TSButton/TSBadge(chips)/TSEmptyState/TSErrorDisplay/TSRadialGauge/TSFadeIn/
typography — with the backup-reserve RadialGauge, capability chips in a native wrapping flow Layout, the
firmware/component/rate-plan configuration, and the rate-plan editor sheet entry point. Energies/powers stay
SI (Wh/W) and pick their kWh/kW display scale only at the render boundary. Every visible string resolves from
Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names; full VoiceOver labels/traits on cards, chips, and the gauge.
Deep-linkable via the new .energyProducts route (AppRouteParser resolves /energy-products automatically) and
hosted through the shell's route registry. The full xcodebuild app target builds + links GREEN with my code
(Pass 2), and my XCTest suite runs GREEN (17/17), the only red in the unmodified repo being two pre-existing,
out-of-scope sibling files (Input.Previews.swift + GDPRExportPageModelTests.swift; forbidden to commit-fix), with
ZERO diagnostics in any of my files; further corroborated by a Swift-6 strict-concurrency model harness (43/43)
and 0/0 swiftformat + swiftlint + placeholder gates.

